                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex 16]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Statement by the United Kingdom Delegation on Article
                        30</hi></head>
                <p>The United Kingdom Delegation attach the greatest importance to the proposals
                    which they have supported in this Article.</p>
                <p>They are concerned that equality of terms should be given to all the United
                    Nations without discrimination, and they consider that this major object can
                    only be assured by the inclusion in the Treaty of words bearing the same meaning
                    as those which they have proposed in regard to participation in Roumanian
                    internal trade, in civil aviation, and in regard to the interpretation of the
                    most-favoured-nation clauses in pre-war Treaties.</p>
            </div>
